00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:30,400
Now as you start as an analytics engineer in a company

29
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:36,000
there are several requirements you need to take care of

30
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:43,992
You want to work in a system where modeling changes are easy to follow and easy to revert

31
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,480
So if you can make your model code it helps a lot

32
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:52,000
because you can version control it right

33
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,000
And you can track all the changes and collaborate and revert

34
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:02,986
You also want to make sure that as you have many steps in your data pipeline

35
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,405
for example many views and tables which feed each other

36
00:03:06,405 --> 00:03:07,994
and depend on each other

37
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,994
you want to make sure that these dependencies are explicit

38
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:16,850
So the framework knows in which order to execute

39
00:03:16,850 --> 00:03:22,992
different steps in your pipeline to get to a well transformed result

40
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,000
a good data set that's ready for analytics

41
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:31,052
Also you want to make sure that it's not only explicit

42
00:03:31,052 --> 00:03:33,999
but it's also easy to overview

43
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,995
So these dependencies are easy to explore easy to overview

44
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:45,077
And this comes with a bunch of feature requirements from a tool

45
00:03:45,077 --> 00:03:47,991
when you build your pipeline

46
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:52,998
So for example a tool should be able to expose this on a UI

47
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,000
And let's see what else

48
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:01,084
You also need to make sure that when your pipeline is working

49
00:04:01,084 --> 00:04:03,989
then you can test for data quality

50
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,994
You can make sure that your pipeline works as expected

51
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:14,992
And if there are any errors then you want to get alerted somehow right

52
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,997
So these are probably the basic requirements

53
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:25,196
And as you will see as we progress in building out our business logic

54
00:04:25,196 --> 00:04:28,983
we will have also a few extra requirements

55
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:34,992
For example we will have tables that are incremental tables so event based tables

56
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:39,000
New events might come in and we don't want to rebuild the whole table

57
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:44,994
We only want to add records add new records at the end of the table

58
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,996
And also in some cases we want to manage slowly changing dimensions

59
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:54,996
That is managing and keeping the history of any change

60
00:04:54,996 --> 00:04:57,992
so we can go back in time

61
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:05,927
So these are some of the main requirements of Data Analytics tool

62
00:05:05,927 --> 00:05:11,990
and dbt is great for managing these requirements

